{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>נשאי המקדש.</b> Bearers of consecrated things." "<b>And they shall set up the Mishkan.</b> The sons of Gershon and the sons of Merari, who preceded them by a march of two banners, would set up the Mishkan when the cloud settled — and the sign of encampment was visible in the banner of the camp of Judah — and while they were encamping, the sons of Kehat were still coming behind them with the two rear banners; the sons of Gershon and the sons of Merari would set up the sanctuary, and when the sons of Kehat arrived they found it in its place, and they brought into it the ark and the table and the menorah and the altars. And this is the meaning of the verse — 'and they that set up the Mishkan shall set it up' <b>until</b> <b>they come</b> — the sons of Kehat."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:10:13.002324233Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}